# AgentRef — environment reference
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in only what you need. The app ships pointing at
# the LIVE deployed GenLayer Intelligent Contract on Testnet — Bradbury
# (src/core/genlayer/contract.ts → LIVE_CONTRACT), so READING the on-chain
# verdict works with no configuration at all.
#
# Env is read in src/core/genlayer/config.ts (client-safe) and
# src/core/genlayer/runtime.ts (server-only).

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GenLayer — the REAL validator path
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Defaults to the live contract, so both lines below are OPTIONAL overrides:
# NEXT_PUBLIC_AGENTREF_CONTRACT_ADDRESS=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_AGENTREF_NETWORK=testnet_bradbury   # testnet_bradbury | testnet_asimov | studionet | localnet
#
# genlayer-js/chains exports are camelCase (testnetBradbury, testnetAsimov,
# studionet, localnet). The network label maps to the right export
# automatically, so you usually do NOT need the next line. Set it only to force
# a different chain than the network default:
# NEXT_PUBLIC_AGENTREF_CHAIN_KEY=testnetBradbury

# Server-only signer for the WRITE path (create_receipt → challenge →
# adjudicate). NEVER prefix with NEXT_PUBLIC_, never commit, never expose to
# the client. Must be a 0x-prefixed 64-hex private key funded on the target
# network (use the official faucet: testnet-faucet.genlayer.foundation).
# Without it the app can still READ the shared on-chain verdict — it just
# cannot sign new adjudications.
# AGENTREF_ACCOUNT_PRIVATE_KEY=
# AGENTREF_ACCOUNT_NAME=agentref
